        "original_id": "aeb97dfb-5e50-5551-aac2-83cff4a9b6f8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Julian Marley\n- Concepts: Rastafari, roots reggae\n- Products: A Time & Place\n- Companies: Lightyear Entertainment\n- Places: Jamaica\n\nFacts:\n- Rastafari is classified as a new religious movement that developed in Jamaica during the 1930s.\n- Roots reggae is a subgenre of reggae that addresses the everyday lives and aspirations of artists, including the spiritual side of Rastafari and the honoring of God as Jah.\n- A Time & Place is the second studio album by Julian Marley, and it was released in 2003 on Lightyear Entertainment.\n- Julian Marley follows in his father’s footsteps and is a devout Rastafarian who uses his music to inspire his life and spirituality.",
